   "source": [
    "# EDA for Gas Monitoring Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "The goal of this notebook is to understand the `gas_monitoring` data before building the machine learning pipeline. The target is `Activity Level`, so I focuse on whether the sensor readings and context columns can help to separate low, moderate and high activity.\n",
    "\n",
    "I also checked for practical data issues first, because the model will only be useful if the pipeline handles messy values properly. In particular, I looked at missing values, inconsistent labels, impossible sensor readings, class imbalance, and which features seems worth to keep."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fecb85fd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## EDA plan\n",
    "\n",
    "| Area checked | Why it matters |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Schema and data types | To know which columns need scaling, encoding or removal |\n",
    "| Missing values | To choose a fair imputation method instead of dropping too many rows |\n",
    "| Dirty labels | To avoid treating the same class as different categories |\n",
    "| Impossible values and outliers | To separate sensor errors from possible real gas spikes |\n",
    "| Target distribution | To see whether accuracy alone would be misleading |\n",
    "| Feature-target relationships | To decide which features and engineered features are useful for modelling |\n",
    "| Pipeline handoff | To make the later cleaning, feature engineering, model and metric choices clear |"
   ]
  },
